Fan project notice
------------------
Hunter x Hunter and its alphabet are (c) Yoshihiro Togashi / Shueisha. HxH OCR is
an unofficial fan project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by them. The
repository contains no images from the manga or the anime. The glyph shapes are
an independent vector tracing, cross-checked against the alphabet charts on
Hunterpedia and Omniglot and against two official charts (not included).

Third-party components
----------------------
Model weights. The released models were fine-tuned from the ImageNet-1k
pretrained weights of timm "mobilenetv4_conv_small_050.e3000_r224_in1k" (the v4
and tiny sets; https://huggingface.co/timm/mobilenetv4_conv_small_050.e3000_r224_in1k)
and "mobilenetv4_conv_small.e2400_r224_in1k" (the base set;
https://huggingface.co/timm/mobilenetv4_conv_small.e2400_r224_in1k), both
Apache-2.0; architecture: MobileNetV4, Qin et al., arXiv:2404.10518.

Fonts in the generated data. The page generator rasterises ordinary writing
and icons from font files read at run time; none are included. The published
datasets used only openly licensed fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1: Noto Sans,
Noto Sans JP / KR / TC / CJK SC, Noto Sans Symbols 2, Noto Emoji, Go Noto
Kurrent, Lato, Inter, Inter Tight, Font Awesome 4.3; Apache-2.0: Roboto, Roboto
Slab, Roboto Mono, Open Sans, GenEi Gothic Pro, Droid Sans Fallback), listed
with versions and hashes in rust/hxh-synth/fonts.lock.json.

Quantisation semantics. hxh-infer and hxh_ocr/qat.py reimplement the int8
arithmetic of Espressif's ESP-DL (MIT) and ESP-PPQ (Apache-2.0); no Espressif
source code is included. The .espdl files under experiments/ were written by
ESP-PPQ.

Rust crates (rust/Cargo.lock). hxh-infer, hxh-detect, hxh-infer-wasm and
hxh-cli have no third-party dependencies; the WebAssembly builds in web/ contain
only this project's code and the Rust core library (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
hxh-synth (the page generator, a build-time tool) uses: ab_glyph,
ab_glyph_rasterizer, owned_ttf_parser (Apache-2.0); ttf-parser, serde,
serde_json, rayon, png, flate2, crc32fast and others (MIT OR Apache-2.0);
tiny-skia, tiny-skia-path (BSD-3-Clause); arrayref (BSD-2-Clause);
zune-jpeg, zune-core (MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR Zlib); jpeg-encoder
((MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND IJG); zlib-rs (Zlib); memchr (Unlicense OR MIT);
unicode-ident ((MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0); strict-num,
simd-adler32, zmij (MIT). See each crate for its licence text.

Python packages (requirements*.txt, installed separately, not distributed):
numpy (BSD-3-Clause), opencv-python (Apache-2.0 / MIT), Pillow (MIT-CMU),
PyTorch and torchvision (BSD-3-Clause), timm (Apache-2.0), onnx (Apache-2.0),
onnxruntime (MIT), onnxscript (MIT), matplotlib (Matplotlib licence, PSF-based),
esp-ppq (Apache-2.0).

Web fonts. The demo and blog load Geist, Geist Mono, Manrope, Noto Sans JP and
Noto Sans Thai from Google Fonts at run time (SIL Open Font License 1.1). No
font files are included in this repository.

Hosting tooling. site/ uses the Cloudflare "cf" CLI as a development
dependency (MIT OR Apache-2.0; its own dependencies include sharp/libvips,
LGPL-3.0-or-later). It is not distributed with the project.
